    "q-142584": {
      "dom_id": "step-q142584",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X$ has a student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom. Given that the random variable $X∼{T}_{10},$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X\\le x)=0.9.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $8$ | $1.397$ | $1.860$ | $2.306$ | $2.896$ | $3.355$ |\n| $9$ | $1.383$ | $1.833$ | $2.262$ | $2.821$ | $3.250$ |\n| $10$ | $1.372$ | $1.812$ | $2.228$ | $2.764$ | $3.169$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The table shows probabilities in the form $P(X\\ge x).$ So first, we express the desired probability in this form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge x) & =1-P(X\\le x) \\\\  & =1-0.9 \\\\  & =0.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{T}_{10},$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=10.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $8$ | $1.397$ | $1.860$ | $2.306$ | $2.896$ | $3.355$ |\n| $9$ | $1.383$ | $1.833$ | $2.262$ | $2.821$ | $3.250$ |\n| $10$ | $1.372$ | $1.812$ | $2.228$ | $2.764$ | $3.169$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 1.372)=0.100.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=1.372.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
