    "q-142492": {
      "dom_id": "step-q142492",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X$ has a student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom. Given that the random variable $X∼{T}_{17},$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(|X|\\le x)=0.99.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $15$ | $1.341$ | $1.753$ | $2.131$ | $2.602$ | $2.947$ |\n| $16$ | $1.337$ | $1.746$ | $2.120$ | $2.583$ | $2.921$ |\n| $17$ | $1.333$ | $1.740$ | $2.110$ | $2.576$ | $2.898$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The table shows probabilities in the form $P(X>x).$ So first, we express the desired probability in this form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(|X|>x) & =1-P(|X|\\le x) \\\\  & =1-0.99 \\\\  & =0.01\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14186989/assets/635de7075b0d106ffc2a0f15e65ca7a3406a49945591aa5eae59090c74df1398.png)\n\nDue to the symmetry of the student's $t$-distribution, we have that $P(|X|>x)=0.01$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\n2P(X>x)=0.01\\,⟹\\,P(X>x)=0.005.\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{T}_{17},$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=17.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $15$ | $1.341$ | $1.753$ | $2.131$ | $2.602$ | $2.947$ |\n| $16$ | $1.337$ | $1.746$ | $2.120$ | $2.583$ | $2.921$ |\n| $17$ | $1.333$ | $1.740$ | $2.110$ | $2.567$ | $2.898$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 2.898)=0.005.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=2.898.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
